# vvaharness/models/provenance.py

The attributable origin of one remediation or one verdict: engine, model, transport, turns, spend and timing. Never holds credential values.

Source: `vvaharness/models/provenance.py` (lines 1-56)
Executor: code
Called from: `vvaharness/models/verdict.py`, `vvaharness/models/remediation.py`, Stage 10 and Stage 11

// src: vvaharness/models/provenance.py:25-27
LLM_REGISTRY = "llm"          // backend prefix for Stage 10 ("llm:<via>")
HARNESS_REGISTRY = "harness"  // backend prefix for Stage 11 ("harness:<via>")

// src: vvaharness/models/provenance.py:30-56
Provenance {
  // frozen; unknown keys ignored
  engine: String = ""          // for example "vvaharness.agentic"
  engine_version: String = ""
  model: String = ""
  backend: String = ""         // registry-qualified transport, for example "llm:cli"; only Stage 10 and Stage 11 stamp it
  // preserved: "llm:deepagents" labels Stage 10 remediation on the deepagents route although that call runs on the
  // harness registry (the llm registry has no deepagents backend and raises on one). It is kept because the
  // (model, backend) pair is hashed into Stage 10 resume checkpoint keys. "harness:deepagents" is Stage 11 validation.
  turns: Number | null = null  // null, not 0, so an unreported count differs from a policy-denied attempt's genuine zero
  usd: Number | null = null
  started: DateTime | null = null   // UTC
  ended: DateTime | null = null     // UTC
}
